# sbt forked test protocol deserialization filter patterns.
# See serialFilterREADME.md in this directory for the file format.
#
# When Ghidra is initialized inside a forked sbt test JVM (e.g. joern's ghidra2cpg tests),
# the JVM-wide filter established from these files also applies to the control socket sbt
# uses to talk to that JVM: at the end of every test run the forked JVM deserializes an
# sbt.ForkTags acknowledgement sent by the sbt process. Without the entries below, that
# read is rejected ("Rejected class serialization(not allowed): sbt.ForkTags") and the
# control socket is torn down, which can fail the whole test task with
# "Forked test harness failed: java.net.SocketException: Broken pipe".

# sbt's forked test protocol messages (sbt.ForkTags, sbt.ForkConfiguration, ...)
sbt.**;

# Superclasses of the sbt.ForkTags enum acknowledgement. Also allowed by
# Ghidra/Features/GhidraServer/data/serial.filter, which is not shipped in this jar.
java.lang.Enum;
java.lang.Object;
